   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "thm:succ_halving",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "If the \\succhalv algorithm of Figure~\\ref{alg:hyperband_infinite} is run with any budget $B > z_{SH}$ then an arm $\\hat{\\imath}$ is returned that satisfies $\\nu_{\\hat{\\imath}} - \\nu_1 \\leq \\epsilon/2$. Moreover, $|\\ell_{\\hat{\\imath},\\lfloor \\tfrac{ B/2 }{ \\lceil \\log_2(n) \\rceil} \\rfloor} - \\nu_1| \\leq \\epsilon$."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Budget sufficient to return an arm with nu - nu_1 <= epsilon/2 (deterministic). Recorded the looser second form of z_SH; the tighter form is 2ceil(log2 n) max_i i(1+gamma_inv(...)). K = n arms."
  },
